# Cultural Scope

- Do not add compositional (Chinese/Japanese/Korean) or circumstantial
  (Akan/Yoruba-style) examples, seed data, or schema assumptions — out of
  scope until a dedicated v2 data model exists.
- Never hardcode "meaning" or "origin" as a single scalar on a name —
  use the `name_enrichments` per-source / per-field shape.
- Keep the `tradition_type` column on `names`. Don't remove it even
  though only `'etymological'` is populated now.
- If a change touches which cultures/languages are represented (UI
  defaults, examples, seed data), don't default to Western examples by
  habit — and don't fabricate low-confidence coverage. Flag the gap
  instead of guessing.
